# Figma-to-NextJS + MUI v6 Conversion Rules

## Styling Governance

- ALL styling MUST use MUI `styled()` API or theme object overrides. No raw CSS, SCSS, Tailwind, or CSS Modules.
- Inline `style={{}}` is forbidden except for truly dynamic computed values (e.g., `style={{ width: calculatedWidth }}`).
- The `sx` prop is acceptable for one-off layout adjustments on MUI components; prefer `styled()` for reusable patterns.
- Every color, spacing, shadow, and typography value MUST originate from the theme or design tokens — no hardcoded hex outside `theme/palette.ts`.

## Theme Architecture

- A centralized theme MUST exist at `src/theme/index.ts` using `createTheme()`.
- Design tokens MUST be split: `palette.ts` (colors/shadows), `typography.ts` (type scale), `components.ts` (MUI overrides).
- Theme MUST wrap the app via `ThemeProvider` in `_app.tsx` or root layout.
- All Figma design tokens (colors, typography, spacing, elevation) MUST be mapped into the theme before component work begins.

## Component Architecture

- Follow atomic design: `atoms/` → `molecules/` → `organisms/` → `templates/` under `src/components/`.
- Each component MUST be a single `.tsx` file (or `index.tsx` inside a named folder).
- Consolidate Figma variants (hover, active, disabled, loading) into ONE functional component using TypeScript props — not separate files.
- Every component MUST export a TypeScript `interface` or `type` for its props (named `<Component>Props`).
- Map Figma Component Properties directly to React props: boolean toggles → boolean props, variant selectors → union type props.

## State Management

- Interactive components (dropdowns, modals, text inputs, toggles) MUST manage internal state via `useState`.
- Side-effect-dependent components MUST use `useEffect` with proper cleanup.
- Controlled component pattern preferred: accept `value` + `onChange` from parent, fall back to internal state when uncontrolled.

## Prop Mapping Contract

- Figma `Show Icon` toggle → `showIcon: boolean`
- Figma `State` (Default/Hover/Active/Disabled/Loading) → handled via CSS states + `disabled` / `isLoading` props
- Figma `Variant` (Primary/Secondary/Text) → `variant: 'contained' | 'outlined' | 'text'`
- Figma `Size` (Small/Medium/Large) → `size: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large'`
- Figma `Icon Position` (Left/Right/None) → `iconPosition: 'start' | 'end' | undefined`

## File Organization

- Barrel exports in `src/components/index.ts` re-exporting all public components.
- Type exports in `src/types/index.ts` re-exporting all prop interfaces.
- `'use client'` directive on every component that uses hooks or browser APIs.
- Path alias `@/` MUST resolve to `./src/` via tsconfig.

## MUI Dependency Requirements

- `package.json` MUST include: `@mui/material` (v6+), `@emotion/react`, `@emotion/styled`.
- `@mui/icons-material` when icons are used.
- `tsconfig.json` MUST have `strict: true`.

## Validation Criteria

- Zero raw CSS files (`.css`, `.scss`, `.sass`, `.less`).
- `styled()` usage count > 0 in component files.
- Every exported component has a corresponding `Props` interface.
- Theme file exists with `createTheme`, `palette`, `typography`, `components`.
- `TypeScript --noEmit` passes with zero errors.
- No `any` types in component props.
